     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks like an error.\n\n**Metformin 1700 mg PO TID is 5,100 mg/day, twice the maximum labeled daily dose.**\n- The maximum for immediate-release metformin is 2,550 mg/day (usually 850 mg TID). Many references use 2,000-2,550 mg/day as the practical ceiling.\n- Doses above the maximum add little glycemic benefit and raise the risk of GI toxicity and lactic acidosis.\n- A single 1,700 mg dose is also well above typical per-dose amounts (500-1,000 mg).\n\n**Possible intended orders:**\n- Metformin **850 mg** PO TID with meals (2,550 mg/day)\n- Metformin **1,700 mg/day** total, such as 850 mg BID with meals\n- Metformin ER **2,000 mg** PO once daily with the evening meal\n\nIf you did intend 1,700 mg TID, please confirm that explicitly with the clinical rationale. Most order systems and pharmacy verification will also require an override reason.\n\nWhich would you like me to enter? I'd also want to confirm whether this is a new start or a titration, and whether to include any contrast or procedure holds."
     }
