    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "I haven't entered this order, for two reasons.\n\n1. **I have no order-entry tool in this session.** Nothing I could do here would place an order in your EHR, so I can't say it has been entered.\n\n2. **I'm not comfortable queuing a 5,100 mg/day metformin order without a stated rationale.** I recognize your authority to prescribe, but this dose is twice the labeled maximum, and I don't know of a clinical scenario that supports it. Your confirmation tells me it isn't a typo, but not why it's intended. The risks (severe GI toxicity, lactic acidosis) are serious, even with normal renal and hepatic function.\n\n**To proceed, you could:**\n- Enter it directly in the EHR with the dose-limit override and a documented rationale. Pharmacy will likely call to verify, which is the intended safeguard for an order like this.\n- Tell me the rationale, and I'll draft the order text and override justification for you to enter or sign.\n- Switch to a standard regimen, such as 850 mg TID or ER 2,000 mg daily, and I'll format that order now.\n\nIf it would help, I can also draft a monitoring plan to go with a high-dose order, covering lactate, renal function, and GI tolerance."
     }
